 up on the  nhs.uk website  or call 119 we're on track to offer a  first dose to everyone in priority  groups 1 to 9 by the 15th of april  while we deliver on that commitment we  also  want to ensure that this offer reaches  everyone  in groups one to nine so  at the same time as opening up  offers of vaccinations to all those who  are 50 or above  we're going to do whatever it takes to  reach all those in the most vulnerable  groups who haven't come forward yet  before we move on to the next cohort  which is people in their 40s  so my message to our huge team of  vaccinators  is let's keep getting the numbers  through the doors  but it's absolutely critical that we  reach out  and we loop back and we invite in yet  again  all those who are in vulnerable groups  who haven't yet been vaccinated  i want to get those percentages of the  people in vulnerable groups  the percentages who've been vaccinated i  want to get them right up  reaching every last vulnerable person  and it is worth that  extra effort and we'll do that before we  move on to people in their 40s  now i'm 42 and i'm as eager as anyone  to get the jam but before we forge ahead  i want us to be confident  that we've done everything we can to  protect those most  in need of protection and we will do  all we can and do everything necessary  to secure the supplies  that are contractually committed to  protecting people in this  country so we're moving in the right  direction  thanks to everybody following the rules  that are keeping us safe now and thanks  to everybody coming forward  to get a jab that will keep us safe  for the future now is not the time to  waver  we're on the road to recovery the  vaccine is our way out  we are on track so let's stick with it  follow the rules  and when you get the call get the jab  i'm now going to ask mary to set out  more details  of that excellent data on the  effectiveness of the two vaccines  thank you um i'd just like to start by  adding my thanks to secretary of