y involved in the  vaccine rollout would agree that we have  that  positive esprit de corps and that's the  best way to leave it  the next question from catherine sampson  at  stv thank you health secretary uh with  the vaccine rollout underway i think a  number of families are really  desperate to find out when they can  reunite with loved ones who live in  different uk  nations now yesterday the first minister  of scotland suggested  cross-border travel restrictions would  ease from around the 26th of april but  she didn't give a firm date so i'm just  wondering do you have a firm day and do  you think it's important  that the whole of the uk moves as one on  this and just on a separate note while  i'm here  just wondering what you made of your  former cabinet colleague david davis's  statement  in the comments yesterday was he right  to use parliamentary privilege to do it  thanks very much so on the first  question um  i very much look forward to at the  uh the all the restrictions on travel  within the uk  being removed i i i that we i've we've  set out  the when the english restrictions will  be removed and we'll  lift uh the uh stay at home  uh message as part of the roadmap out uh  and i've no doubt that within  a short few weeks uh everybody will be  free to travel around  the uk so long as we're able to keep  this progress going both the progress in  the uk wide vaccination effort  and keeping the number of cases under  control  when it comes to the what my colleague  david davis said in the house he's a  very experienced parliamentarian very  long-standing  um it is absolutely right and proper to  be able to use parliamentary privilege  in the way that he did parliamentarians  should give  due consideration before using  parliamentary privilege  and i'm sure that he did that um the  next question from jason groves at the  daily mail  thanks health secretary uh you skated  over uh  this issue of a falling vaccine supply  like it's some kind of technical is